\f0\b\fs26 \cf2 SCOPE\
\f1\b0\fs22 \
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 Chanta-only slice of the Rock Against Revival sequence: green-room confrontation with the High Elvis over lyrics \uc0\u8594  tower climb \uc0\u8594  the vision \uc0\u8594  the self-belief/placebo mechanism \uc0\u8594  text \uc0\u8594  rush back to the green room. Nothing from scenes 1, 2, 3 or 5 belongs here except as established backdrop (cited below). Do not restage the crowd/bands/three laws (scene 1), the platform/thrones/Eloise\'92s arrival (scene 2), or the Sages\'92 ukulele hijack (scene 3) \'97 reference them only glancingly, in passing, as concurrent offstage action.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa51\partightenfactor0\cf2 \
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 STEP-BY-STEP BEATS (in order \'97 do not reorder or add)\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 1. Establish where Chanta has been all day: per scene 2\'92s brief, he \'93doesn\'92t want to face Sarah, doesn\'92t join her on the platform, spends most of the day carousing with bands and Elvisettes in the green room \'97 this is where his throne stays visibly empty.\'94 This scene opens inside or returns to that state; do not re-derive it from scratch, just carry it forward.\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 2. As the High Elvis\'92s closing set nears, the High Elvis finds Chanta in the green room and raises the lack of lyrics: verbatim author phrase, preserve \'97 \'93there would have been less fighting if there were more lyrics.\'94 He wants one song about the Dawkins/evolution, to help turn the tide against the Holy Rollers, and needs it to close the set on.\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 3. Chanta has been despondent about Sarah and Little Clinton all day (carry forward from beat 1 \'97 this is the same despondency, not a new mood swing).\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 4. He goes to the engineering tower. His own stated (and wrong) reason: he believes he needs to be nearer to Sarah/the baby for inspiration. This is his private muse-theory talking, not the narrator endorsing it \'97 see CANON below.\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 5. On the tower, what he actually thinks about is not Sarah: it\'92s how the Holy Rollers wrecked the Memphis Mafia Bar and are wrecking the Ghetto.\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 6. He looks at the setting sun; it triggers his recurring vision of Little Clinton as an orange ball of light in Sarah\'92s belly. No new icon is needed or wanted here (no balloon, no glowing baby prop) \'97 the sun alone does the work, as it always has for this motif.\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 7. Out-of-body experience: psychotropics + cocktail sugar. He \'93flies\'94 down and occupies his (empty) throne beside Sarah\'92s \'97 purely visionary. His body never leaves the tower; it stays slumped there, scribbling. \'93Chanta never goes on\'94 \'97 preserve this exact framing; he does not physically go to the platform or the stage anywhere in this scene.\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 8. From that god\'92s-eye vantage: the realisation that it isn\'92t only the Holy Rollers he must speak against. The Evolution Elvi worship Sarah and Little Clinton as \'93The One After the One\'94 \'97 equally religious, equally credulous. He must speak against ALL religious minds.\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 9. Lyrics come too fast to catch. He grabs a notepad from beside the sound desk (establishes the tower is a working production position \'97 sound/lighting desk, per scene 2\'92s \'93engineering tower (for sound/lighting/production coordination)\'94) and scribbles.\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 10. He texts the High Elvis: \'93I have a song.\'94\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 11. He rushes back \'97 specifically to the GREEN ROOM. Not the tower (he\'92s leaving it), not the platform. This exact destination is specified by the brief; do not substitute the stage or the platform.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa51\partightenfactor0\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa51\partightenfactor0
\f0\b\fs26 \cf2 POV / TONE\
\f1\b0\fs22 \
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 Close third on Chanta throughout. Voice per chanta.md\'92s Voice section: mental vacuum, urchin cunning, internal register sardonic, self-deprecating even under pressure \'97 do not let the vision push him into unbroken solemnity. The precedent is his first vision, in \'93Let Your Momma Go\'94 (orange glow, Little Clinton \'93curled within,\'94 followed immediately by the deflating \'93I could really go a cheeseburger\'94) \'97 verified against established-facts.md\'92s Chanta entry. This scene needs the same bathos reflex somewhere in or immediately after the vision \'97 cosmic flight and mundane deflation in the same breath is the house style for this character\'92s epiphanies, not a one-off.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa51\partightenfactor0\cf2 \
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 Author\'92s own tonal flag, protect hard: \'93this bit is very Tom Robbins.\'94 Read as: treat the metaphysical (flying to occupy a throne, a god\'92s-eye view of half a million worshippers) with cheerful matter-of-factness rather than reverence or portentous weight; keep circumstantial, physical specificity running underneath the cosmic leaps (a notepad beside a sound desk, a phone, the sugar-crash of a novelty cocktail) rather than letting the prose float off into pure abstraction.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa51\partightenfactor0\cf2 \
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 The dramatic irony is structural, not stated. Per chanta.md decisions-log \'a7J (verified verbatim against source file): the reader must catch the gap between what Chanta believes is happening (Sarah/Little Clinton as muse, granting him the song) and what is actually happening (his own innate talent, permission-via-belief, occasioned by rage at the Bar and a clear-eyed look at the worshipping crowd \'97 nothing to do with the baby). Do NOT have Chanta articulate this gap to himself or anyone else. He \'93will attribute it to Little Clinton (he always does)\'94 \'97 the misattribution is his, and it should read as sincere, not a lie he\'92s telling himself and knows is a lie. The narration can let the reader see the seams (e.g., the actual content of the lyrics being plainly about the Bar and the crowd, not the baby) without Chanta ever noticing them.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa51\partightenfactor0\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa51\partightenfactor0
\f0\b\fs26 \cf2 CANON THIS SCENE MUST NOT CONTRADICT\
\f1\b0\fs22 \
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 \uc0\u8226  The muse-theory is false and this scene is where it\'92s finally, quietly disproven on the page, per chanta.md decisions-log \'a7J (2026-07-11) and part5-close-decisions-log.md \'a7J. Direct quotes to hold to, both verified verbatim: \'93Chanta\'92s writing talent is innate: his knack for naming the obvious thing everyone else steps around... He needs neither Sarah nor Little Clinton \'97 he only believes he does, and that false belief is the sole thing limiting him\'94; \'93the psychotropic vision that seems to deliver the song is Chanta unconsciously manufacturing the muse\'92s presence to grant himself permission\'97a placebo.\'94 Do not let the prose endorse the muse theory as true, even implicitly, even in mystical vision-logic.\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 \uc0\u8226  DECOUPLED from the reunion \'97 part5-close-decisions-log.md \'a7J, author\'92s own words, verified verbatim: \'93My read of the story does not link Sarah and Chanta\'92s reconciling to him writing Religious Minds... Do not tie his songs to seeing Sarah.\'94 The vision is not a reunion and must not read as one \'97 Sarah on the platform is unaware this is happening; there is no exchange, no eye contact, no acknowledgement from her side. Her cutaway reaction belongs to scene 5\'92s performance, not to this private vision.\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 \uc0\u8226  Prior instalments of the same running motif, which this scene closes out \'97 do not contradict any of them: the orange-glow/Little-Clinton vision originates in \'93Tony\'92s health improves, and he goes to buy coffee.\'94 / is first fully theorised in \'93Let Your Momma Go\'94 (\'93perhaps the secret to his creative wellspring had always been Sarah\'92s growing baby\'94); the false belief is restated at the Penthouse nadir (chanta.md: \'93Songwriter\'92s block... which Chanta himself blames on Sarah\'92s absence... his private muse-theory. The story disproves it: he wrote \'91Let Your Momma Go\'92 after she left\'94); the contradiction is flagged again in \'93Tony & the Elvi research the Dawkins\'94 (\'93Muse-theory contradiction deepening: believes creativity requires Sarah\'92s presence, yet produces doggerel and triggers cultural transformation without her\'94). This scene is the terminal beat \'97 the contradiction finally gets its (unspoken) explanation.\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 \uc0\u8226  The Memphis Mafia Bar\'92s conversion into Rex Humble\'92s \'93New Graceland\'94 is already-established fact, not something to re-explain from scratch: humble.md and lonnie.md (\'93Her workplace, the Memphis Mafia Bar, is converted into Rex Humble\'92s \'91New Graceland\'92 \'97 the cost of the gospel arc\'94). Chanta\'92s rage here is about something the reader has already seen happen, not a new revelation of plot.\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 \uc0\u8226  The High Elvis\'92s register: \'93Stays in his counselling register throughout, never bombast\'94 (the-high-elvis.md) \'97 even pressing Chanta for a song, he should read as calm and pastoral, not commanding or panicked. This matches Scene 1\'92s \'93calm and counselling, never bombast\'94 note carried across the whole night.\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 \uc0\u8226  Chanta does not perform. \'93Chanta never goes on\'94 is an explicit constraint from the brief \'97 his songwriting labour is always offstage/backstage; whoever eventually performs \'93Religious Minds\'94 in scene 5 is not resolved here and is not this scene\'92s problem.\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 \uc0\u8226  No Sages here. Per the brief: their entire presence in this concert sequence is scene 3\'92s ukulele hijack; do not have them appear on or near the tower, in the green room, or anywhere in this scene.\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 \uc0\u8226  No Dunhilton/Gerry cutaway. That reaction (grinding teeth, three emergency dental visits) is explicitly relocated to the later, separate Occupy Bent Street / Get Bent! scene. Do not pre-empt it here.\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 \uc0\u8226  No island-of-irony framing, no Sages on/beneath the tower, no Gyges-disc experiment, no \'93irony above a sea of faith,\'94 no crowd-convergence-into-unison ending \'97 all retracted per the task brief and must not resurface in any form, including as atmosphere or metaphor.\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 \uc0\u8226  No floating-foetus/glowing-baby balloon icon. The recurring vision is achieved through the sun alone, as it always has been; Colonel Tom Porker (the floating pig, established in scene 2) belongs to that scene\'92s staging, not this one \'97 see OPEN QUESTIONS below re: whether he\'92s glimpsed here at all.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa51\partightenfactor0\cf2 \
