\f0\b\fs26 \cf2 WHAT THIS SCENE SETS UP\
\f1\b0\fs22 \
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 \uc0\u8226  Scene 5\'92s announcement: \'93the Great Teacher has written new material, never played before \'97 a song called \'91Religious Minds.\'92\'94 This scene is the direct, immediate cause of that announcement (the text: \'93I have a song\'94).\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 \uc0\u8226  Scene 5\'92s thematic content: the song is against \'93religious minds\'94 plural, not just the Holy Rollers, because of the realisation reached on the tower (beat 8) \'97 this is why the finished song can plausibly also indict the Evolution Elvi\'92s own worship of Sarah and Little Clinton, which is what licenses Sarah\'92s cutaway reaction in scene 5 (\'93hears an accusation she can\'92t answer\'94).\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 \uc0\u8226  The book\'92s larger thematic rhyme, per chanta.md \'a7J: \'93the man who writes the anthem against religious minds has the most religious mind in the book \'97 a congregation of one, kneeling to Sarah\'92s belly \'97 and never recognises his own irony,\'94 which rhymes with \'93the crowd never recognises \'91Praise the Dawkins\'92\'94 from scene 3. This scene is where that rhyme is planted; it is not paid off or explained on the page here.\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 \uc0\u8226  Carry-forward legal/rights flag (originates in this scene, since this is where the song is written, though the fuller flag and its context sit with scene 5\'92s performance): \'93Religious Minds\'94 tracks \'93Suspicious Minds\'94 (Mark James, 1968) closely in structure and phrasing \'97 satire of religion, not parody of the song, which is the weaker fair-use footing. Not a craft problem to solve in prose; flag for the publisher\'92s rights team.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa51\partightenfactor0\cf2 \
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 OPEN QUESTIONS FOR THE DRAFTER (brief does not resolve these \'97 do not invent answers that read as new plot; pick the lightest-touch option)\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 \uc0\u8226  Actual lyrics: the brief does not give any lines of \'93Religious Minds,\'94 unlike the Sages\'92 ditty (scene 3), which is reproduced verbatim. \'93Lyrics come too fast to catch\'94 licenses withholding the words entirely here \'97 recommend gesturing at content/imagery only (rage, the gutted Bar, the god\'92s-eye view of the crowd) without composing finished verses, and deferring the actual lyric text to scene 5\'92s performance (which the brief also does not fully specify beyond the cutaway structure).\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 \uc0\u8226  Tower staffing/blocking: scene 2 establishes the tower as a working sound/lighting/production position. Is Chanta alone up there, or does he have to get past or ignore crew at the sound desk? The brief only says he grabs a notepad \'93beside the sound desk,\'94 which implies a desk but not whether anyone is at it.\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 \uc0\u8226  Timing pressure: \'93as the High Elvis\'92s closing set nears\'94 implies some urgency, but the brief doesn\'92t specify how much real time elapses between the green-room confrontation and the text arriving. Leave loose rather than inventing a countdown \'97 note this also governs the handoff into Scene 5 (the text needs to land during, not before, the High Elvis\'92s set for the mid-set announcement to make sense).\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 \uc0\u8226  Physical route up/down the tower and back to the green room: unspecified \'97 stairs, ladder, lift; leave to drafter, keep consistent with an \'93engineering tower\'94 rather than anything more exotic.\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 \uc0\u8226  Colonel Tom Porker (established overhead throughout the night in scene 2): whether he\'92s visible/glimpsed from the tower is not specified by the brief for this scene. Flagging per the brief\'92s own instruction to flag rather than invent \'97 treat as optional ambient continuity at most, not a beat this scene owes.\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 \uc0\u8226  Exact nature of \'93psychotropics\'94 is not specified beyond \'93psychotropics + cocktail sugar\'94 \'97 scene 1\'92s cocktails are established as sweet/fatty with very little alcohol; whether Chanta\'92s psychotropic state comes from those cocktails, from something else consumed while carousing in the green room, or both, is not stated. Do not over-explain the pharmacology on the page.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa51\partightenfactor0\cf2 \
